# state.pdl - every file rmmc may leave beside its book, and what kind of fact it is (no ghost data, owner 2026-11-07).
# Each row names the line I saw it written at (2026-11-25 review, plan section 5 item 1).
# FILE | name | kind | writer | regenerate_with
FILE | rmmc-pchq/pieces/system/maps/rmmc/rmmc-0000/ | PROJECTION | rmmc_field_op writes cells.rgba (rmmc_field_op.c:95 to :99), cells.txt (:101), map.txt (:103), extrusion.pdl (:125), events.txt (:131, emptied), cells.marker (:133, APPENDS one byte per run: it grows, so it is not a pure projection; restart it on regenerate), skin.txt (:135) | rmmc_field_op <tileset_dir> <desk_dir>
FILE | rmmc-pchq/pieces/system/maps/rmmc/rmmc-0001/ | PROJECTION | rmmc_scale_op makes it from the centroid small page; rmmc_biome_op repaints cells.txt, map.txt, extrusion.pdl, legend.txt, cells.rgba, events.txt (empty), cells.marker (size = old mod 4000 + 1) from biomes.pdl (2026-11-25) | rmmc_scale_op <centroid small> <desk> 3 then rmmc_biome_op biomes.pdl <desk>
FILE | biomes.pdl | CONFIG | hand-edited biome rows (the only place the island numbers live); never written by an op | none
